AN ORDINANCE REPEALING ARTICLE VII OF CHAPTER 14 OF THE WARREN COUNTY CODE PERTAINING TO NUISANCES AND ADOPTING A NEW ORDINANCE PERTAINING TO NUISANCES IN CHAPTER 18 OF THE CODE AND PROVIDING FOR THE CONTROL AND ABATEMENT OF NUISANCES

WHEREAS, the Warren County Board of Commissioners has determined there are dwellings, buildings or structure conditions in Warren County which are of the character described in O.C.G.A. § 41-2-7;

WHEREAS, pursuant to the authority granted by Article IX, Section II, Paragraph III(a)(12) of the Georgia Constitution, O.C.G.A. § 36-13-1, and O.C.G.A. §§ 41-2-7 et seq., the Board of Commissioners desires protect the public health, safety, morals, and the general welfare of the County’s residents;

WHEREAS, the Board of Commissioners desires to accomplish this goal in part by providing authorization and adopting procedures pursuant for the abatement of nuisances within Warren County;

NOW, THEREFORE, the Board of Commissioners hereby enacts this Ordinance pertaining to nuisances and their abatement as follows:
